==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} ''[[échalote]]'', alteration of ''eschaloigne'', from Middle Latin ''escalonia'' "onion of [[w:Ascalon|Ascalon]]".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈʃælət/|/ʃəˈlɑt/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ʃəˈlɒt/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒt}}
{{rfap|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A vegetable in the onion family.
## ''[[Allium ascalonium]]''.
## ''[[Allium oschaninii]]''.
## Any small onion.
## {{context|New Orleans}} A [[scallion]]

